## Source
Path B UX dry-run (0152), severity: **Medium**

## Context
The README's verification section says run `erg version` and compare its printed
sha256 to what you see. But `erg version` generates its sha256 *from itself* —
there is no independent reference hash. For a fresh `curl` download this is
self-attestation only; a tampered binary would pass its own check.

The README acknowledges signed release tags will be available "from 2026-05-30
onwards" but that future state is not yet in place.

## Fix
Two options (not mutually exclusive):
1. Note explicitly in the verification section that `erg version` / `sha256sum`
   only confirms no corruption in transit; authenticity requires a signed release
   tag (link to where those will appear).
2. Publish sha256 hashes alongside each GitHub release so a fresh downloader has
   an independent reference to compare against.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Verification docs accurately describe what `erg version` does and does not prove
